# Public repository

`shotsmith` is a public MIT project. Anyone can read every file, commit, release note, and Actions log. Write it for those readers. The private repository is `shotsmith-pro`. Do not treat the public repo as a scratchpad for the private one.

## Belongs here

What the app does, how to build it, how to contribute, how to check a download, and a short statement that Pro is separate and not in this tree.

## Does not belong here

- Publishing setup: certificates, Apple ID, notarization passwords, Actions secret names or values, and the steps used to sign or ship a release. The release workflow may use secrets. Do not document that setup in the README, release notes, or comments.
- Private product material: the PRD, unpublished prices, internal plans, and anything copied from `shotsmith-pro`.
- Chat: questions, answers, plans, transcripts, and prompts. Answer those in the conversation. Put text in this repo only when the user asks for that text in the repo.
- Personal details (job, family, biography) unless the user asks for that exact text in the repo.

```text
Bad:  A README section that lists signing secret names and how to export the certificate
Good: README says installers are on Releases and how to check SHA256SUMS

Bad:  Commit a rewritten chat answer about pricing or signing
Good: Reply in chat. Leave the public docs unchanged.
```

Before committing, read the diff. If it contains a secret name used as instructions, a price, a PRD excerpt, or chat wording, delete it. Do not push unless the user asked to push.
